ChapelSort.jl is an independent Julia reimplementation of the design of
Chapel's standard library sort; no Chapel source code is included. The
following files follow Chapel's design, structure and parameter choices and
are marked as modified derivatives in their headers:

    src/two_array.jl     Chapel modules/standard/Sort/TwoArrayPartitioning.chpl
                         and TwoArrayRadixSort.chpl (parallel two-array
                         partitioning: per-task counts, bucket-major prefix
                         sum, scatter, big/small task queues)
    src/serial_msd.jl    Chapel modules/standard/Sort/MSBRadixSort.chpl
                         (serial MSD radix sort for small subproblems)
    src/keys.jl          Chapel modules/standard/Sort.chpl, defaultComparator
                         key parts (order-preserving unsigned keys)
    src/strings.jl       Chapel modules/standard/Sort.chpl, string key parts
                         (byte-wise keys with an end-of-string marker)
    src/psort.jl         Chapel modules/standard/Sort.chpl (dispatch between
                         the serial and parallel radix sorts by input size)
    bench/chapel/sortbench.chpl
                         benchmark from the Chapel blog post "Comparing
                         Standard Library Sorts: The Impact of Parallelism"
                         (M. Ferguson, 2024)

